# Code Audits (audit-kit)

When the user asks to run an audit, review code quality, or execute `/audit`:
1. Read `audit-kit/RUN.md` fully before starting.
2. Follow the requested mode (Standard by default, Full when requested, Diff for PRs/merges).
3. Audit agents and tools are strictly read-only: write findings exclusively to `audit/`. Never edit project code during an audit.
4. Use `audit-kit-agent: <name>` headers and keep dimension findings isolated from one another.
5. Verify Critical and High findings with the skeptic verifier (`audit-kit/agents/skeptic-verifier.md`).
6. Generate `audit/AUDIT.md`, `audit/findings.json`, run `python3 audit-kit/tools/generate_tracker.py` for Excel tracking, and `python3 audit-kit/tools/generate_dashboard.py` for the interactive HTML dashboard (`audit/dashboard.html`).
